(4618832, 655620, 68035, '<td valign="top">Wow.  I have to say that I am not a big portrait fan in free studies, but occasionally DPC throws up an image that just stops you in your tracks and leaves your speechless<br/> <br/>This is one of those shots<br/> <br/>Love the fact that even though you have gone for only a half face portraitt (my favourite) that you have got it filling the screen so well<br/> <br/>Love the high key and the outstanding shapness.<br/> <br/>Terrific B&amp;W conversion<br/> <br/>9 from me</td>', 'Wow.  I have to say that I am not a big portrait fan in free studies, but occasionally DPC throws up an image that just stops you in your tracks and leaves your speechless This is one of those shots Love the fact that even though you have gone for only a half face portraitt (my favourite) that you have got it filling the screen so well Love the high key and the outstanding shapness. Terrific B&W conversion 9 from me', '2008-04-06 17:51:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4618835, 655093, 68035, '<td valign="top">oooooo struggling a bit with this shot....<br/> <br/>I love the composition, the star burst effect and the sharpness, but the difference in hues on the left and the right I find to be quite distracting and rather than adding to the shot detracts a bit (just my opinion and fortunately I am not the global artbiter of taste!).  Id love to see this as a strong b&amp;W</td>', 'oooooo struggling a bit with this shot.... I love the composition, the star burst effect and the sharpness, but the difference in hues on the left and the right I find to be quite distracting and rather than adding to the shot detracts a bit (just my opinion and fortunately I am not the global artbiter of taste!).  Id love to see this as a strong b&W', '2008-04-06 17:55:56.000000', NULL, 1),
